{"id":15683,"artist":"Garth Brooks","title":"If Tomorrow Never Comes","lyrics_plain":"Sometimes late at night\nI lie awake and watch her sleeping\nShe's lost in peaceful dreams\nSo I turn out the lights\nAnd lay there in the dark\nAnd the thought crosses my mind\nIf I never wake in the morning\nWould she ever doubt the way I feel\nAbout her in my heart\nIf tomorrow never comes\nWill she know how much I loved her\nDid I try in every way \nTo show her every day\nThat she's my only one\nAnd if my time on earth were through\nAnd she must face this world without me\nIs the love I gave her in the past\nGonna be enough to last\nIf tomorrow never comes\n'Cause I've lost love ones in my life\nWho never knew how much I loved them\nNow I live with the regret\nThat my true feelings for them never were revealed\nSo I made a promise to myself\nTo say each day how much she means to me\nAnd avoid that circumstance\nWhere there's no second chance to tell her how I feel\nCause if tomorrow never comes\nWill she know how much I loved her\nDid I try in every way to show her every day\nThat she's my only one\nAnd if my time on earth were through\nAnd she must face this world without me\nIs the love I gave her in the past\nGonna be enough to last\nIf tomorrow never comes\nSo tell that someone that you love\nJust what you're thinking of\nIf tomorrow never comes\n","lyrics_synced":"[00:08.57] Sometimes late at night\n[00:14.14] I lie awake and watch her sleeping\n[00:23.57] She's lost in peaceful dreams\n[00:26.14] So I turn out the lights and lay there in the dark\n[00:35.57] And the thought crosses my mind\n[00:41.36] If I never wake up in the morning\n[00:51.43] Would she ever doubt the way I feel\n[00:55.93] About her in my heart\n[01:02.57] If tomorrow never comes\n[01:09.86] Will she know how much I loved her\n[01:16.71] Did I try in every way to show her every day\n[01:23.79] That she's my only one\n[01:29.79] And if my time on earth were through\n[01:36.64] And she must face the world without me\n[01:43.29] Is the love I gave her in the past\n[01:47.57] Gonna be enough to last\n[01:51.00] If tomorrow never comes\n[01:57.21] 'Cause I've lost loved ones in my life\n[02:03.86] Who never knew how much I loved them\n[02:13.29] Now I live with the regret\n[02:15.86] That my true feelings for them never were revealed\n[02:25.29] Made a promise to myself\n[02:31.07] To say each day how much she means to me\n[02:41.14] And avoid that circumstance\n[02:44.14] Where there's no second chance to tell her how I feel\n[02:52.29] If tomorrow never comes\n[02:59.57] Will she know how much I loved her\n[03:06.43] Did I try in every way to show her every day\n[03:13.50] That she's my only one\n[03:19.50] And if my time on earth were through\n[03:26.36] And she must face the world without me\n[03:33.00] Is the love I gave her in the past\n[03:37.29] Gonna be enough to last\n[03:40.71] If tomorrow never comes\n[03:46.93] So tell that someone that you love\n[03:51.21] Just what you're thinking of\n[03:54.21] If tomorrow never comes\n","lyrics_synced_enhanced":"[00:08.57] <00:08.57>Some <00:09.00>times <00:09.85>late <00:10.07>at <00:10.28>ni <00:10.50>ght\n[00:14.14] <00:14.14>I <00:14.57>lie <00:14.78>a <00:15.00>wake <00:15.85>and <00:16.07>watch <00:16.50>her <00:17.14>sleep <00:18.42>ing\n[00:23.57] <00:23.57>She's <00:24.00>lost <00:24.42>in <00:24.64>peace <00:25.07>ful <00:25.50>dre <00:25.60>ams\n[00:26.14] <00:26.14>So <00:26.57>I <00:27.00>turn <00:27.42>out <00:27.85>the <00:28.07>lights <00:28.92>and <00:29.14>lay <00:29.35>there <00:30.00>in <00:30.21>the <00:30.42>dark\n[00:35.57] <00:35.57>And <00:35.78>the <00:36.00>thought <00:36.42>cross <00:36.85>es <00:37.28>my <00:37.71>mind\n[00:41.35] <00:41.35>If <00:41.57>I <00:42.00>nev <00:42.21>er <00:42.42>wake <00:42.85>up <00:44.14>in <00:44.35>the <00:44.57>morn <00:45.85>ing\n[00:51.42] <00:51.42>Would <00:51.85>she <00:52.28>ev <00:52.50>er <00:52.71>dou <00:52.92>bt <00:54.42>the <00:54.64>way <00